nFXFHwV' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-09-28 02:08:30.793 xcodebuild[67262:29278476]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-09-28 02:08:30.961 xcodebuild[67262:29278475] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\nbb.edn\nshadow-cljs.edn\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/ws.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/serving.cljc\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/connect.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc\ntest/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc\ntest/dao/stream/rpc_test.cljc\ntest/dao/stream/rpc_ws_test.cljc\ntest/dao/stream/serving_test.cljc\ntest/dao/stream/slice_peer.cljc\ntest/dao/stream/slice_test.clj\ntest/dao/stream/slice_test.cljd\ntest/dao/stream/slice_test.cljs\ntest/dao/stream/ws/node_test.cljs\ntest/yin/repl/adapter_test.cljc\ntest/yin/repl/connect_test.cljc\ntest/yin/repl/driver_test.cljc\ntest/yin/repl/embed_test.cljc\ntest/yin/repl/main_test.cljc\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc\ntest/yin/repl/slice_peer.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_parity_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_contract_test.cljc\nBoth P1s are fixed in the two slice-8 files only (both still untracked; no git operations).\n\n**Finding 1 — lowered link waits now park where the engine polls.**\n- `lower-one` stamps the entry with the engine's own fixed keys: `:request module/link-request-resource`, `:response module/link-response-resource` (src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:693-694), and a new `link-pair-resources` (remote.cljc:591-617, merged at remote.cljc:741-744) installs the pair's reflections under exactly those keys — so the engine's retry append (`module/append-link-request`, module.cljc:403) and response poll (`poll-link-response`, engine.cljc:1215) find them. The lift correspondingly reads the pair through the entry's own ids, which are those fixed keys on the engine's entries (`lift-link` docstring, remote.cljc:368-379). Link cells still lower under the cell id (S7.5.3 sharing preserved).\n\n**Finding 2 — a retained FFI request now travels with its response route.**\n- Lift: new `call-out-cell` (remote.cljc:309-325) resolves the emitter's fixed call-out keys (`vm/call-out-cursor-key` → `{:stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key, :cursor kept}`); `lift-retained-request` (remote.cljc:328-362) mints it through the frame-wide cell mint — so it dedupes with a co-waiting `:ffi` response wait on the same cursor (S7.5.3) — and adds `:yin.k/response-cell`; `:cell? true` now puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in requires. A missing pair or non-round-tripping cursor refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied`.\n- Lower: `route-cells` (remote.cljc:543) + `cursor-entry-key` (remote.cljc:553) lower the route cell AS the fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key` entry onto the fixed `vm/call-out-stream-key` reflection (remote.cljc:527-540), so the restored response wait and every co-reader advance one shared entry; `call-pair-resources` (remote.cljc:562-587) installs the reflections at the receiver's fixed call-in/call-out keys; the `:ffi-request` entry parks with `:stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key` (remote.cljc:674). `semantic-restore`'s response wait (semantic.cljc:106-115) therefore polls the receiver's working pair and receives the retried response.\n\n**Tests added/updated** (test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc):\n- `a-lowered-link-request-retries-and-resumes-through-the-engine` (:441): a real machine parked by `(require ...)` with its request stream full — new `one-slot-stream` helper (:175), the one append outcome a ring buffer never gives; the lower parks on the fixed keys; receiver run 1 performs the engine's own retry (the retained envelope verified landing verbatim on the emitter's request stream through the mirror/wire) and polls the response reflection; run 2 resumes — halted with the module's own value, empty wait-set.\n- `a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes` (:499): a real `:request-sent` park; asserts the route cell at the kept call-out position, the fixed-key installations, run 1's retry (envelope verified on the emitter's call-in via the wire), and run 2 resuming the parked call with the correlated response (`\"echo!\"`), empty wait-set.\n- `link-request-round-trips`, `link-response-round-trips`, `ffi-retained-round-trips` updated to the fixed-key shapes (they were asserting the broken identity-derived keys); `server` gained a surfaces arity (`#{:reader :writer}` for remote-writable streams); `quiesced-receiver` gained a machine arity (the linked-meanwhile registry).\n\n**Lane counts.**\n- JVM (`clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`): Ran 18 tests containing 149 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Node (`shadow-cljs` build, `node target/node-tests.js --test=yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`): Ran 18 tests containing 149 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Dart (`flutter test test/cljd-out/yin/vm/ucf/remote-test_test.dart` on the `cljd`-compiled file): 18 of 18 passed, 0 failures.\n- Attribution of full-suite failures observed during verification (NOT this slice): full Node run (2173 tests/49765 assertions) — 7 failures, all in `dao.stream.ws.node-test`, the concurrent slice-5 ws/rpc in-flight work (`rpc.cljc`, `ws_project.cljc` modified, `rpc/ws.cljc` deleted); full Dart run — 17 failures, all demo/embed loading failures from the same in-flight work and the shared `cljd-out` tree mid-rebuild (`lib/cljd-out/cljd/flutter.dart` IFnMixin errors emitted by the concurrent run). My namespace is green on every lane.\n- Hygiene: cljstyle check clean, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings, pure ASCII, all lines ≤ 80 columns, no leftover diagnostics; no commit/stage/checkout/reset/stash performed.\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
