tep 5b against the live\\n  1165\\t   state and, discharged, starts the install child, the entry becoming\\n  1166\\t   an `:install` waiter. A module linked or installing meanwhile answers\\n  1167\\t   or joins instead, and a manifest naming another module than the one\\n  1168\\t   required is `:module-name-mismatch`, never installed. Returns `[state\\n  1169\\t   waiting woken]`.\\\"\\n  1170\\t  [state entry response]\\n  1171\\t  (let [state (retire state (:link-id entry) :restored)\\n  1172\\t        module-name (:name entry)\\n  1173\\t        waiter (-> entry\\n  1174\\t                   (dissoc :envelope :request :response :cursor :link-id)\\n  1175\\t                   (assoc :reason :install))]\\n  1176\\t    (cond\\n  1177\\t      (not= :ok (:status response))\\n  1178\\t      [state nil (refused-entry entry response)]\\n  1179\\t\\n  1180\\t      (some? (module/resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\\n  1181\\t      [state nil (ready entry module-name)]\\n  1182\\t\\n  1183\\t      (contains? (:installs state) module-name) [state waiter nil]\\n  1184\\t\\n  1185\\t      ;; the linker checks the name (section 8.1); a response that names\\n  1186\\t      ;; another module is never installed under this one\\n  1187\\t      (not= module-name (get-in response [:manifest :yin.module/name]))\\n  1188\\t      [state nil\\n  1189\\t       (refused-entry entry\\n  1190\\t                      (linker/refused :module-name-mismatch\\n  1191\\t                                      {:requested module-name,\\n  1192\\t                                       :manifest (get-in\\n  1193\\t                                                   response\\n  1194\\t                                                   [:manifest\\n  1195\\t                                                    :yin.module/name])}))]\\n  1196\\t\\n  1197\\t      :else\\n  1198\\t  (let [[state waiting woken]\\n  1199\\t        (reduce (fn [[state waiting woken] entry]\\n  1200\\t                  (let [[state w k] (poll-link-entry state entry)]\\n  1201\\t                    [state\\n  1202\\t                     (cond-> waiting w (conj w))\\n  1203\\t                     (cond-> woken k (conj k))]))\\n  1204\\t                [state [] []]\\n  1205\\t                links)]\\n  1206\\t    (-> state\\n  1207\\t        (assoc :wait-set (into (vec others) waiting))\\n  1208\\t        (update :ready-queue (fnil into []) woken)\\n  1209\\t        advance-installs)))\\n  1210\\t\\n  1211\\t\\n  1212\\t(defn abandon-link\\n  1213\\t  \\\"A composition gives up on link `link-id` (section 7.2, step 7): the\\n  1214\\t   entry leaves the wait set and is restored with `reason` raised as the\\n  1215\\t   effect's error; the id is retired, so a response arriving later is\\n  1216\\t   `:late`. The linker side's `abandon` is the composition's call. An id\\n  1217\\t   no entry holds leaves the state unchanged.\\\"\\n  1218\\t  [state link-id reason]\\n  1219\\t  (let [held? (fn [e]\\n  1220\\t                (and (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} (:reason e))\\n  1221\\t                     (= link-id (:link-id e))))]\\n  1222\\t    (if-let [entry (first (filter held? (:wait-set state)))]\\n  1223\\t      (-> state\\n  1224\\t          (update :wait-set (fn [ws] (filterv (complement held?) ws)))\\n  1225\\t          (retire link-id :abandoned)\\n  1226\\t          (update :ready-queue (fnil conj [])\\n  1227\\t                  (refused-entry entry\\n  1228\\t                                 {:status :lost,\\n  1229\\t                                  :reason reason,\\n  1230\\t                                  :link-id link-id})))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '940,962p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | nl -ba -v940\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '940,962p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | nl -ba -v940\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   940\\tone entry and one ref per cell keeps its own. The FFI response cell of\\n   941\\t§7.4.3 is a cell like any other.\\n   942\\t\\n   943\\t**Cells lower into the private resource table (linker M4).** Specified by\\n   944\\t`yin.vm.linker.md` and implemented in M4. The lowering rule above -- each\\n   945\\tcell becomes a fresh store cursor entry -- is amended by the resource\\n   946\\tsplit of `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3: each cell becomes a cursor entry in the\\n   947\\treceiver's private `:resources` table, seeded with its carried position,\\n   948\\tand every `:yin.k/cursor-ref` to it remaps to that entry; two refs to one\\n   949\\tcell still share one entry and one ref per cell keeps its own, but no\\n   950\\tstore key is ever created, and program values keep only the opaque\\n   951\\treference ids, exactly as a running program holds them.\\n   952\\t\\n   953\\tA stream reference is portable when the exporter can enter its handle in a\\n   954\\t`dao.stream.remote.md` table and publish a remote descriptor for the\\n   955\\toriginal logical stream. This applies to local implementations,\\n   956\\tincluding an in-memory or string-backed stream; they need no native\\n   957\\tnetwork transport. The exporter checks the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor\\n   958\\tprofile before encoding the cell, and the receiver holds a reflection\\n   959\\tafter `attach!`. The mirror preserves the source's cursor and outcome\\n   960\\tsemantics, including `gap`; it does not turn `:oldest` or `:newest` into\\n   961\\ta kept position. A raw host handle\\n   962\\tstill never crosses the value boundary. A stream that cannot be served or\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 17:29:05 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 00:29:05 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\n\\n**Slice 8 verdict: request changes.** The two files contain the reported real-entry lift, codec round-trip check, and frame-wide cell sharing. The supplied 16-test/106-assertion result is green, but two lowered waits cannot resume correctly through the current engine:\\n\\n- **Link waits use keys the engine does not read.** [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:535) lowers the link pair under identity-derived resource IDs. The engine polls the response at the fixed `module/link-response-resource` key ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1215)), and request retry uses the fixed `link-request-resource` key ([module.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:403)). The link round-trip tests check fields and resource presence, but never poll a lowered link wait ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:604)).\\n- **A retained FFI request loses its response route.** [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:292) lifts only the request stream and creates no response cell; [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:520) lowers that request accordingly. After the retry succeeds, `semantic-restore` creates a response wait on the receiver’s fixed local call-out keys ([semantic.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:132)). A response to the migrated request arrives on the emitter’s pair, so that wait is stranded. The test checks the rebuilt envelope but does not resume the retry ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:577)).\\n\\nI did not edit files or rerun suites. The reported full-lane slice-5 and slice-peer failures are outside this gate.\\n\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\\nSign-off: DENIED\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":290052,\"cached_input_tokens\":245120,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1851,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":85}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
