{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '300,590p'\"","aggregated_output":"   300\t  (let [call-in (one-slot-stream \"call-in\")\n   301\t        call-out (ring 8)\n   302\t        _ (stream/append! call-in :warmed)\n   303\t        datoms (caller-datoms op arg)\n   304\t        parked (vm/run (load-ast (calling-machine call-in call-out)\n   305\t                                 datoms))\n   306\t        entry (first (:wait-set parked))]\n   307\t    [datoms parked entry call-in call-out]))\n   308\t\n   309\t\n   310\t(defn- registers-of\n   311\t  \"The register payload a parked entry carries.\"\n   312\t  [entry]\n   313\t  (select-keys entry [:segment :pc :env :stack :k]))\n   314\t\n   315\t\n   316\t(defn- quiesced-receiver\n   317\t  \"The fresh engine state a lower installs into: a real machine over\n   318\t   the same code image, quiesced, holding the lowered resource table\n   319\t   and the lowered wait-set entry -- nothing of the emitter's state\n   320\t   but the code image and the registers the entry carries.\"\n   321\t  ([datoms lowered] (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered (new-machine)))\n   322\t  ([datoms lowered machine]\n   323\t   (assoc (load-ast machine datoms)\n   324\t          :control nil, :k nil,\n   325\t          :value :yin/blocked, :blocked? true, :halted? false,\n   326\t          :wait-set [(:entry lowered)],\n   327\t          :resources (:resources lowered))))\n   328\t\n   329\t\n   330\t(defn- cursor-entries\n   331\t  \"The cursor entries of a lowered resource table: maps keyed by the\n   332\t   UCF cell ids, each carrying its stream id and kept cursor.\"\n   333\t  [table]\n   334\t  (into {} (filter (fn [[_ v]] (and (map? v) (contains? v :stream-id))))\n   335\t        table))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t;; =============================================================================\n   339\t;; The acceptance row: a real parked machine migrates and resumes\n   340\t;; =============================================================================\n   341\t\n   342\t(deftest migrates-a-real-parked-machine-and-resumes\n   343\t  (let [t (toy)\n   344\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   345\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\n   346\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   347\t        [datoms parked entry src] (parked-reader 4)\n   348\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\n   349\t        sid (:stream-id entry)\n   350\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\n   351\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   352\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   353\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   354\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   355\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\n   356\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine\"\n   357\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\n   358\t      (is (= :next (:reason entry)))\n   359\t      (is (= :cursor-ref (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :type]))))\n   360\t    (testing \"the lift reads the engine's own wait-set entry\"\n   361\t      (is (= {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell :yin.k/c-0}\n   362\t             (:yin.k/pending lifted))\n   363\t          \"the cursor CELL id, S7.5.3 -- not a bare position\")\n   364\t      (is (= kept (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\n   365\t          \"the cell carries the engine's kept cursor\")\n   366\t      (is (= #{:dao.stream.remote/v1}\n   367\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/requires :yin.k/cursor-profiles]))))\n   368\t    (testing \"the lower builds a fresh engine state\"\n   369\t      (let [e (:entry lowered)\n   370\t            rs (:resources lowered)\n   371\t            cid' (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])\n   372\t            sid' (:stream-id e)]\n   373\t        (is (= (registers-of entry) (registers-of e))\n   374\t            \"the register context rides the lower verbatim\")\n   375\t        (is (not= cid cid'))\n   376\t        (is (not= sid sid'))\n   377\t        (is (not (contains? rs cid)))\n   378\t        (is (not (contains? rs sid)))\n   379\t        (is (= {:stream-id sid', :cursor kept} (get rs cid'))\n   380\t            \"one fresh cursor entry, at the kept position\")\n   381\t        (is (not= src (get rs sid'))\n   382\t            \"the stream entry is a reflection, not the emitter's handle\")\n   383\t        (is (= sid' (get-in rs [cid' :stream-id])))))\n   384\t    (testing \"the emitter's own wait resumes equivalently\"\n   385\t      (stream/append! src \"hello\")\n   386\t      (is (= \"hello\" (vm/value (vm/run parked)))))\n   387\t    (testing \"the migrated wait resumes in the fresh engine state\"\n   388\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\n   389\t          \"the reflection answers blocked until the mirror serves\")\n   390\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\n   391\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\n   392\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\n   393\t        (is (= \"hello\" (vm/value done))\n   394\t            \"the source's own value, through the kept cursor\")\n   395\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\n   396\t\n   397\t\n   398\t(deftest forced-eviction-yields-gap-with-the-sources-cursor\n   399\t  (let [t (toy)\n   400\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   401\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t))\n   402\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   403\t        [datoms parked entry src] (parked-reader 2)\n   404\t        cid (:id (:cursor-ref entry))\n   405\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\n   406\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   407\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   408\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   409\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   410\t        cid' (get-in (:entry lowered) [:cursor-ref :id])\n   411\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\n   412\t    (stream/append! src \"hello\")\n   413\t    (doseq [v [\"v1\" \"v2\" \"v3\"]]\n   414\t      (stream/append! src v))\n   415\t    (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver)))\n   416\t    (serve-mirror! peer)\n   417\t    (let [expected (stream/next src kept)\n   418\t          done (vm/run receiver)]\n   419\t      (testing \"the program reads the source's own gap, verbatim\"\n   420\t        (is (= :dao.stream/gap (vm/value done)))\n   421\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor expected)\n   422\t               (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor]))\n   423\t            \"with the source's own recovery cursor in the cell\"))\n   424\t      (testing \"no replay and no silent skip: the walk continues\n   425\t                from the recovery cursor\"\n   426\t        (let [r (get-in done [:resources (:stream-id (:entry lowered))])\n   427\t              recovery (get-in done [:resources cid' :cursor])]\n   428\t          (is (= :dao.stream/blocked\n   429\t                 (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next r recovery))))\n   430\t          (serve-mirror! peer)\n   431\t          (let [ok (stream/next r recovery)]\n   432\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome ok)))\n   433\t            (is (= \"v2\" (:dao.stream/value ok)))))))))\n   434\t\n   435\t\n   436\t;; =============================================================================\n   437\t;; The fixed keys: lowered link waits and retained FFI requests\n   438\t;; resume through the engine's own poll and retry paths\n   439\t;; =============================================================================\n   440\t\n   441\t(deftest a-lowered-link-request-retries-and-resumes-through-the-engine\n   442\t  (let [t (toy)\n   443\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   444\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\n   445\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   446\t        [datoms parked entry req-src resp-src]\n   447\t        (parked-requirer 'host.the-module)\n   448\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   449\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   450\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   451\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   452\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   453\t        e (:entry lowered)\n   454\t        rs (:resources lowered)\n   455\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered\n   456\t                                    (linked-machine 'host.the-module))]\n   457\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine, envelope retained\"\n   458\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\n   459\t      (is (= :link-request (:reason entry)))\n   460\t      (is (= module/link-request-resource (:request entry)))\n   461\t      (is (= module/link-response-resource (:response entry)))\n   462\t      (is (map? (:envelope entry)) \"the request the retry appends\"))\n   463\t    (testing \"the lower parks the wait where the engine polls\"\n   464\t      (is (= module/link-request-resource (:request e))\n   465\t          \"the retry appends at the engine's fixed request key\")\n   466\t      (is (= module/link-response-resource (:response e))\n   467\t          \"the poll reads at the engine's fixed response key\")\n   468\t      (is (contains? rs (:request e)))\n   469\t      (is (contains? rs (:response e))\n   470\t          \"the pair's reflections stand under the fixed keys\"))\n   471\t    (testing \"the engine's own poll retries and resumes the require\"\n   472\t      ;; the linker answered before the migration: the response sits\n   473\t      ;; on the emitter's response stream, past the kept cursor\n   474\t      (stream/append! resp-src\n   475\t                      {:status :ok,\n   476\t                       :yin.link/id (:link-id entry),\n   477\t                       :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.the-module}})\n   478\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\n   479\t          \"first poll: the envelope is retried, the answer not yet read\")\n   480\t      (let [w0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   481\t                 (stream/cursor req-src :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   482\t        (is (= :warmed\n   483\t               (:dao.stream/value (stream/next req-src w0)))\n   484\t            \"reading the warm-up frees the slot the retry needs\"))\n   485\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\n   486\t      (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   487\t                 (stream/cursor req-src :dao.stream/oldest))\n   488\t            r (stream/next req-src c0)]\n   489\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   490\t        (is (= (:envelope entry) (:dao.stream/value r))\n   491\t            \"the envelope verbatim, appended via the fixed request key\"))\n   492\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\n   493\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\n   494\t        (is (= 'host.the-module (vm/value done))\n   495\t            \"the require resumes with the module's own value\")\n   496\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\n   497\t\n   498\t\n   499\t(deftest a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes\n   500\t  (let [t (toy)\n   501\t        peer (served-peer t)\n   502\t        serve! (server peer (:channel t) #{:reader :writer})\n   503\t        attach! (attacher t)\n   504\t        [datoms parked entry call-in-src call-out-src]\n   505\t        (parked-caller :op/echo \"hello\")\n   506\t        kept (get-in parked [:resources vm/call-out-cursor-key :cursor])\n   507\t        lifted (ucf.remote/lift-pending serve! (:resources parked) entry)\n   508\t        pending (:yin.k/pending lifted)\n   509\t        lowered (ucf.remote/lower-pending attach! pending\n   510\t                                          (:yin.k/cells lifted)\n   511\t                                          (registers-of entry))\n   512\t        e (:entry lowered)\n   513\t        rs (:resources lowered)\n   514\t        receiver (quiesced-receiver datoms lowered)]\n   515\t    (testing \"the machine parked through the engine, request retained\"\n   516\t      (is (vm/blocked? parked))\n   517\t      (is (true? (:request-sent entry)))\n   518\t      (is (= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id entry)))\n   519\t      (is (apply2/request? (:datom entry))))\n   520\t    (testing \"the lift carries the response route as a cell\"\n   521\t      (is (= :yin.k/c-0 (:yin.k/response-cell pending)))\n   522\t      (is (= kept\n   523\t             (get-in lifted [:yin.k/cells :yin.k/c-0 :yin.k/position]))\n   524\t          \"the emitter's call-out cursor at its kept position\"))\n   525\t    (testing \"the lower installs the route on the receiver's keys\"\n   526\t      (is (= vm/call-in-stream-key (:stream-id e))\n   527\t          \"the retry appends at the engine's fixed call-in key\")\n   528\t      (is (= {:stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key, :cursor kept}\n   529\t             (get rs vm/call-out-cursor-key))\n   530\t          \"the route cell lowers AS the fixed call-out cursor\")\n   531\t      (is (contains? rs vm/call-out-stream-key)\n   532\t          \"the response wait reads the reflection at the fixed key\"))\n   533\t    (testing \"the retried response resumes the parked call\"\n   534\t      ;; the bridge answered before the migration: the response sits\n   535\t      ;; on the emitter's call-out stream, past the kept position\n   536\t      (stream/append! call-out-src\n   537\t                      (apply2/success-response (:call-id entry)\n   538\t                                               \"echo!\"))\n   539\t      (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run receiver))\n   540\t          \"first round: the request is retried, the response not yet\n   541\t           read\")\n   542\t      (let [w0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   543\t                 (stream/cursor call-in-src :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   544\t        (is (= :warmed\n   545\t               (:dao.stream/value (stream/next call-in-src w0)))\n   546\t            \"reading the warm-up frees the slot the retry needs\"))\n   547\t      (serve-mirror! peer)\n   548\t      (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   549\t                 (stream/cursor call-in-src :dao.stream/oldest))\n   550\t            r (stream/next call-in-src c0)]\n   551\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   552\t        (is (= (:datom entry) (:dao.stream/value r))\n   553\t            \"the retained request verbatim, via the fixed call-in key\"))\n   554\t      (let [done (vm/run receiver)]\n   555\t        (is (vm/halted? done))\n   556\t        (is (= \"echo!\" (vm/value done))\n   557\t            \"the restored response wait received the retried response\")\n   558\t        (is (empty? (:wait-set done)))))))\n   559\t\n   560\t\n   561\t;; =============================================================================\n   562\t;; Unsatisfied: an unpublishable cursor, a source that cannot be\n   563\t;; served, a gone reflection\n   564\t;; =============================================================================\n   565\t\n   566\t(defn- host-cursor-stream\n   567\t  \"A handle whose cursors hold a host object -- the case\n   568\t   dao.stream.remote.md S2.3 says cannot be served.\"\n   569\t  []\n   570\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   571\t    (descriptor\n   572\t      [_]\n   573\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   574\t       :dao.stream/identity \"host-cursor\"\n   575\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\n   576\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n   577\t        :dao.stream/identity \"host-cursor\"}})\n   578\t\n   579\t\n   580\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   581\t\n   582\t    (cursor\n   583\t      [_ _]\n   584\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   585\t       :dao.stream/cursor {:position 0, :owner (fn [x] x)}})\n   586\t\n   587\t    (next\n   588\t      [_ _]\n   589\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n   590\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'S7\\\\.5\\\\.3|shared.*cell|sharing rule|response-cell' docs src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:7:   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:20:   share the one entry, S7.5.3), and wait-set entries that merge the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:77:   cells stay independent (S7.5.3, and the sharing rule of the S7.11\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:210:;; Cell minting and remapping (S7.5.3), across the whole frame set\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:218:   stay independent, whatever their positions (S7.5.3). `k` is the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:339:   (S7.5.3). `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when the request stream cannot be\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:357:                   :yin.k/response-cell cid},\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:437:   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:526:   and one ref per cell keeps its own (S7.5.3). A response-route cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:548:   response wait -- share the one entry (S7.5.3).\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:550:  (into #{} (keep :yin.k/response-cell) pendings))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:577:                                            (:yin.k/response-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:666:          route-id (cell-identity cells (:yin.k/response-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:713:   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3) --\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:5561:Decisions: Used event/bind over streams (the artifact demo's pattern) rather than calling the pure `step`. Runtime focus is set at boot and cleared on host blur, which cancels held keys. Buttons are drawn as DOM (cljs) and widgets (cljd) from the shared layout, NOT as postgraphics ops: the WebGPU submitter (`web/gpu.cljs` submit-webgpu!) encodes only :mesh-3d/:mesh-textured-3d/:line-3d and silently drops :draw-2d, :text and :draw3d/triangles, so in-frame 2D ops would be invisible wherever navigator.gpu exists. The user flagged that this is not fully postgraphics. Open decision, nothing built: (1) implement 2D and text in the WebGPU submitter, then draw the controls with :draw/* ops and delete the overlays (recommended; needs a real-GPU check), or (2) draw them as ortho :draw3d/mesh quads (small, opaque, works everywhere now). dao.gui.event drops the raw :cancel for a single-contact press (pointer/process-cancel reads the arena after remove-contact; process-up reads it before), so a cancelled touch would leave a button held: the runner releases a button on any pointer up or cancel instead. The interpreter is unchanged; the fix would mirror process-up and may touch fixtures. Committed on a new branch because master is the default branch; not merged.\ndocs/datomic.md:340:* **A mutable, shared cell.** The *values* are plain Clojure maps (`{:id key :v buf ...}`), but the *store* must be a map inside a mutable, atomic container so a `put` is observable by a later `get`. `KVMem` uses a `ConcurrentMap`; an `atom` wrapping a persistent map would do equally well. A bare immutable map cannot be a `KVStore` — it has no identity-preserving mutation.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1765:  cursor cells advance independently, and shared cells advance in wait\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790522276329-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm.gpt-6-sol.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790522276329-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm.gpt-6-sol.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 17:29:05 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 00:29:05 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**Slice 8 verdict: request changes.** The two files contain the reported real-entry lift, codec round-trip check, and frame-wide cell sharing. The supplied 16-test/106-assertion result is green, but two lowered waits cannot resume correctly through the current engine:\n\n- **Link waits use keys the engine does not read.** [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:535) lowers the link pair under identity-derived resource IDs. The engine polls the response at the fixed `module/link-response-resource` key ([engine.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1215)), and request retry uses the fixed `link-request-resource` key ([module.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:403)). The link round-trip tests check fields and resource presence, but never poll a lowered link wait ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:604)).\n- **A retained FFI request loses its response route.** [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:292) lifts only the request stream and creates no response cell; [remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:520) lowers that request accordingly. After the retry succeeds, `semantic-restore` creates a response wait on the receiver’s fixed local call-out keys ([semantic.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:132)). A response to the migrated request arrives on the emitter’s pair, so that wait is stranded. The test checks the rebuilt envelope but does not resume the retry ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:577)).\n\nI did not edit files or rerun suites. The reported full-lane slice-5 and slice-peer failures are outside this gate.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
