{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '1,390p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote\n     2\t  \"The UCF facade through `dao.stream.remote` descriptors: lifts a\n     3\t   parked semantic machine's pending wait\n     4\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3) into\n     5\t   UCF data whose cells and stream markers name `dao.stream.remote`\n     6\t   descriptors under the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile\n     7\t   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\n     8\t   through a reflection (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2,\n     9\t   S2.4).\n    10\t\n    11\t   The local side is the engine's own parked machinery, not an\n    12\t   invented shape. A pending entry is what `yin.vm` parks: the\n    13\t   machine registers beside `:stream-id` and `:cursor-ref`\n    14\t   (`yin.vm.semantic` S3.5's park entries, `response-wait-entry`;\n    15\t   `yin.vm.engine`'s wait-set sweep), every handle and cursor\n    16\t   resolved out of the machine's private `:resources` table -- the\n    17\t   lift reads the table, and no entry ever carries a live handle.\n    18\t   The lower mirrors it: fresh resource entries, one per stream\n    19\t   reflection and one per cursor cell (two waiters sharing one cell\n    20\t   share the one entry, S7.5.3), and wait-set entries that merge the\n    21\t   caller's register context verbatim, so a lowered wait parks under\n    22\t   the engine's own sweep exactly as an unmigrated one does.\n    23\t\n    24\t   Where the engine polls a wait at one of its own fixed resource\n    25\t   keys, the lower installs the reflections under exactly those keys\n    26\t   and stamps them on the entry, so the engine's poll and retry paths\n    27\t   find what they look for, and the lift reads the same keys back:\n    28\t   the link pair (`yin.vm.module`'s link-request-resource and\n    29\t   link-response-resource), and the FFI call pair (`yin.vm`'s\n    30\t   call-in-stream-key, call-out-stream-key and call-out-cursor-key --\n    31\t   a retained request's response route, carried as a cell so the\n    32\t   restored response wait finds the retried response).\n    33\t\n    34\t   `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` are plain-data functions,\n    35\t   parameterized by two composition callbacks rather than coupled to\n    36\t   `yin.vm` or `dao.stream.remote` internals:\n    37\t\n    38\t     serve!  : handle -> {:dao.stream/identity id\n    39\t                          :dao.stream/channel chan} | nil\n    40\t               the exporter's own table entry\n    41\t               (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3): nil when the handle\n    42\t               cannot be served -- no table to enter it in, no\n    43\t               channel to the resumer -- which refuses the lift as\n    44\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before minting the value\n    45\t               (S7.4.3).\n    46\t\n    47\t     attach! : remote-descriptor -> {:dao.stream/outcome\n    48\t                                     :dao.stream/ok\n    49\t                                     :dao.stream/handle reflection}\n    50\t               | outcome-map\n    51\t               the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach` dispatch for\n    52\t               `:dao.stream/remote` (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.4): an\n    53\t               outcome other than `ok` -- including a reflection\n    54\t               already marked gone -- refuses the lower as\n    55\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream identity.\n    56\t\n    57\t   The `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim is checked, not declared: a cell\n    58\t   is published only after its kept cursor survives a round trip\n    59\t   through the channel codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which\n    60\t   is what plain data in the channel's portable domain means\n    61\t   (S7.4.3; `dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3's plain-data basis).\n    62\t   `cursor-codec` is the default codec; a composition whose channel\n    63\t   speaks another passes its own `{:encode f :decode f}` to\n    64\t   `lift-pending` or `lift-frame`. A cursor that does not round trip\n    65\t   -- a host object inside is the case S2.3 names -- refuses the lift\n    66\t   as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value is minted.\n    67\t\n    68\t   Every pending variant of S7.4.3 lifts and lowers: `:next`, `:put`,\n    69\t   `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`, and the linker's `:link-request`,\n    70\t   `:link-response` and `:install` (`yin.vm.linker.md` S7.2-7.3).\n    71\t   `:install` names no stream and passes through unchanged.\n    72\t\n    73\t   Scope: `lift-frame` and `lower-frame` are the frame-level entry\n    74\t   points -- cells are minted and remapped across the WHOLE entry\n    75\t   set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to one UCF\n    76\t   cell and lower back into one shared cursor entry, and independent\n    77\t   cells stay independent (S7.5.3, and the sharing rule of the S7.11\n    78\t   pending-state blocker). `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` lift or\n    79\t   lower one entry into a self-contained table.\"\n    80\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    81\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    82\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n    83\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    84\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\t(def cursor-profiles\n    88\t  \"The one portable cursor profile S7.4.3 names in :yin.k/requires: a\n    89\t   cursor is plain data in the channel's portable domain and the\n    90\t   source honors it after serialization, cursor identity, position and\n    91\t   `gap` outcomes included.\"\n    92\t  #{:dao.stream.remote/v1})\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(def cursor-codec\n    96\t  \"The channel codec a lift round-trips kept cursors through when the\n    97\t   composition supplies none: the DaoStream v2 wire codec, whose\n    98\t   portable domain is the domain the profile claim names.\"\n    99\t  {:encode cbor/encode, :decode cbor/decode})\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(def ^:private requires\n   103\t  {:yin.k/cursor-profiles cursor-profiles})\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t;; =============================================================================\n   107\t;; Markers (S7.5.1), through a remote descriptor\n   108\t;; =============================================================================\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- local-identity\n   111\t  \"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\n   112\t   nil otherwise -- the best name a refusal can give when `serve!` has\n   113\t   not minted one.\"\n   114\t  [h]\n   115\t  (let [d (when (stream/descriptor? h) (stream/descriptor h))]\n   116\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d))\n   117\t      (:dao.stream/identity d))))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- unsatisfied\n   121\t  ([] (unsatisfied nil))\n   122\t  ([identity]\n   123\t   (cond-> {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied}\n   124\t     (some? identity) (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity))))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- portable-cursor\n   128\t  \"The kept cursor when it survives a round trip through the channel\n   129\t   codec -- encoded, decoded back, and equal -- which is what the\n   130\t   `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim means: plain data in the channel's\n   131\t   portable domain, honored after serialization. nil when it does\n   132\t   not, so no cell is ever published over an unpublishable cursor.\"\n   133\t  [codec cursor]\n   134\t  (try (let [w (:encode codec)\n   135\t             b (w cursor)\n   136\t             r ((:decode codec) b)]\n   137\t         (when (= cursor r) cursor))\n   138\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn lift-marker\n   142\t  \"The UCF stream marker (S7.5.1) for local handle `h`, its descriptor\n   143\t   the remote descriptor `serve!` mints by entering `h` in the\n   144\t   exporter's table (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2). nil when `serve!`\n   145\t   refuses -- the source cannot be entered, or cannot honor the\n   146\t   profile -- so a caller mints `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value\n   147\t   is produced (S7.4.3).\"\n   148\t  [serve! h]\n   149\t  (when-let [served (serve! h)]\n   150\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity served)]\n   151\t      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\n   152\t       :dao.stream/identity id,\n   153\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\n   154\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\n   155\t        :dao.stream/identity id,\n   156\t        :dao.stream/channel (:dao.stream/channel served)}})))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t(defn lower-marker\n   160\t  \"The local handle `attach!` gives for UCF stream marker `m` -- a\n   161\t   reflection on the original logical stream -- or nil when the attach\n   162\t   does not answer ok: a reflection marked gone, or any other refusal,\n   163\t   is unsatisfied at the caller.\"\n   164\t  [attach! m]\n   165\t  (let [result (attach! (:dao.stream/descriptor m))]\n   166\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   167\t      (:dao.stream/handle result))))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t;; =============================================================================\n   171\t;; The pending wait (S7.4.3)\n   172\t;; =============================================================================\n   173\t;;\n   174\t;; Local pending-entry shapes this namespace lifts, and lowers back to\n   175\t;; -- the engine's own wait-set shapes, plain data resolved through\n   176\t;; the machine's `:resources` table:\n   177\t;;\n   178\t;;   {:reason :next          :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\n   179\t;;                           :stream-id sid}          ; blocked read\n   180\t;;   {:reason :next          :call-id id :op op        ; a sent call's\n   181\t;;                           :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\n   182\t;;                           :stream-id sid}          ; response wait\n   183\t;;   {:reason :put           :stream-id sid            ; blocked write,\n   184\t;;                           :datom v}                 ; :datom the retry\n   185\t;;   {:reason :put           :request-sent true        ; a retained FFI\n   186\t;;                           :call-id id :op op        ; request; the\n   187\t;;                           :stream-id sid :datom env}; fixed call-in\n   188\t;;   {:reason :link-request  :link-id id :name m :envelope e\n   189\t;;                           :request rid :response rid' :cursor kept}\n   190\t;;   {:reason :link-response :link-id id :name m\n   191\t;;                           :request rid :response rid' :cursor kept}\n   192\t;;   {:reason :install       :name m}\n   193\t;;\n   194\t;; `cid` names a `:resources` cursor entry `{:stream-id sid :cursor\n   195\t;; kept}` (`vm/cursor-entry`); `sid` and `rid` name stream handles in\n   196\t;; the same table; `env` is the retained `dao.stream.apply` envelope.\n   197\t;; On a real entry the retained request's `sid` is the engine's fixed\n   198\t;; `vm/call-in-stream-key`, and a link wait's `rid`/`rid'` are the\n   199\t;; fixed `module/link-request-resource` and\n   200\t;; `module/link-response-resource` -- the keys the engine's own retry\n   201\t;; and poll paths resolve.\n   202\t;; The registers every parked entry also carries -- :segment :pc :env\n   203\t;; :stack :k -- are the machine's own context: the lift ignores them\n   204\t;; (they travel in the frame's continuation slice, not the pending\n   205\t;; wait), and the lower stamps the caller's context back onto the\n   206\t;; entry it builds.\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\t;; =============================================================================\n   210\t;; Cell minting and remapping (S7.5.3), across the whole frame set\n   211\t;; =============================================================================\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn- mint-cell\n   214\t  \"One mint per distinct cursor cell across the WHOLE frame set:\n   215\t   `found` accumulates the remapping {cell key -> UCF cell id} beside\n   216\t   the cells themselves as entries lift, so two waiters on one\n   217\t   engine cursor cell lift to one UCF cell, and independent cells\n   218\t   stay independent, whatever their positions (S7.5.3). `k` is the\n   219\t   cell's identity -- the engine cursor resource id a `:next` waiter\n   220\t   names, or the response stream and kept cursor a link wait names.\n   221\t   The cell carries the marker `serve!` mints for the cell's stream\n   222\t   and its kept cursor, published only after the cursor survives the\n   223\t   codec round trip; nil -- refuse -- when it does not, or when\n   224\t   `serve!` refuses the stream.\"\n   225\t  [serve! found]\n   226\t  (fn [codec k handle kept]\n   227\t    (or (get-in @found [:of k])\n   228\t        (let [portable (portable-cursor codec kept)\n   229\t              marker (when portable (lift-marker serve! handle))]\n   230\t          (when (and portable marker)\n   231\t            (let [cid (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"c-\" (count (:cells @found))))\n   232\t                  cell {:yin.k/stream marker, :yin.k/position portable}]\n   233\t              (swap! found #(-> % (assoc-in [:of k] cid)\n   234\t                                (assoc-in [:cells cid] cell)))\n   235\t              cid))))))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn- cursor-cell\n   239\t  \"The engine cursor cell a `:next` entry waits on: `:cursor-ref`'s\n   240\t   id into `:resources`, the cursor entry carrying the stream id and\n   241\t   the kept cursor (`vm/cursor-entry`). nil when it names nothing.\"\n   242\t  [resources entry]\n   243\t  (let [cid (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id])\n   244\t        cell (get resources cid)]\n   245\t    (when (and (some? cid) (map? cell) (contains? cell :stream-id))\n   246\t      {:id cid, :stream-id (:stream-id cell), :cursor (:cursor cell)})))\n   247\t\n   248\t\n   249\t(defn- cell-identity\n   250\t  \"The stream identity a `:yin.k/cells` entry names, for a refusal\n   251\t   that names it even when the cell itself never lowered.\"\n   252\t  [cells cell-id]\n   253\t  (get-in cells [cell-id :yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity]))\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\t;; =============================================================================\n   257\t;; Lift: one variant each\n   258\t;; =============================================================================\n   259\t\n   260\t(defn- lift-read\n   261\t  \"S7.4.3's blocked read: the cell `mint` gives for the entry's\n   262\t   cursor cell, at its kept position.\"\n   263\t  [resources mint codec entry]\n   264\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\n   265\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\n   266\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\n   267\t                       (:cursor cell))]\n   268\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell cid}, :cell? true}\n   269\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\n   270\t    (unsatisfied)))\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\t(defn- lift-response-wait\n   274\t  \"S7.4.3's sent call: a `:next` entry carrying `:call-id`, the\n   275\t   response wait `semantic-restore` rebuilds -- the call's\n   276\t   correlation beside the response cell at its kept position, so\n   277\t   round-order on the cell is preserved on the resumer (S7.4.3).\n   278\t   The call's `:op` rides when the entry carries it (the engine's\n   279\t   own response wait does not; a caller assembling the frame takes\n   280\t   it from the call's parked record).\"\n   281\t  [resources mint codec entry]\n   282\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\n   283\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\n   284\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\n   285\t                       (:cursor cell))]\n   286\t      {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi,\n   287\t                         :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   288\t                         :yin.k/cell cid}\n   289\t                  (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry))),\n   290\t       :cell? true}\n   291\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\n   292\t    (unsatisfied)))\n   293\t\n   294\t\n   295\t(defn- lift-write\n   296\t  \"S7.4.3's blocked write: the target stream's marker and the\n   297\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\n   298\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\n   299\t   cursor cell.\"\n   300\t  [serve! resources entry]\n   301\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\n   302\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   303\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\n   304\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\n   305\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\n   306\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   307\t\n   308\t\n   309\t(defn- call-out-cell\n   310\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route a retained\n   311\t   request's retry reads through. Once the request lands, the engine\n   312\t   restores the call as a response wait parked on its fixed local\n   313\t   call-out keys (`semantic-restore` -> `response-wait-entry`), so\n   314\t   the route is the cursor entry under `vm/call-out-cursor-key`,\n   315\t   reading the call-out stream under `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its\n   316\t   kept position. nil when the composition holds no call pair, which\n   317\t   no real retained request does -- the pair is checked before the\n   318\t   call parked.\"\n   319\t  [resources]\n   320\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n   321\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n   322\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n   323\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\n   324\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   325\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- lift-retained-request\n   329\t  \"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\n   330\t   the request the engine holds unsent. The request stream's marker\n   331\t   is served, and `:request-op` and `:request-args` are read out of\n   332\t   the retained envelope so a resumer rebuilds it verbatim under the\n   333\t   call id. The response route rides beside them as a cell: the\n   334\t   emitter's call-out cursor (`call-out-cell`) at its kept position --\n   335\t   once the retry lands, the response is read on the emitter's\n   336\t   call-out stream through it, so a resumer without the cell strands\n   337\t   the restored response wait. The cell shares by identity like any\n   338\t   other: a response wait on the same call-out cursor lifts to it too\n   339\t   (S7.5.3). `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when the request stream cannot be\n   340\t   served, or the route is missing or its cursor does not survive the\n   341\t   codec round trip.\"\n   342\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   343\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\n   344\t        envelope (:datom entry)\n   345\t        route (call-out-cell resources)]\n   346\t    (if-let [cid (when route\n   347\t                   (mint codec (:id route)\n   348\t                         (get resources (:stream-id route))\n   349\t                         (:cursor route)))]\n   350\t      (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   351\t        {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\n   352\t                   :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   353\t                   :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n   354\t                                         (:op entry)),\n   355\t                   :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\n   356\t                   :yin.k/request marker,\n   357\t                   :yin.k/response-cell cid},\n   358\t         :cell? true}\n   359\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))\n   360\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity\n   361\t                     (or (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))\n   362\t                         h))))))\n   363\t\n   364\t\n   365\t(defn- lift-link\n   366\t  \"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\n   367\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\n   368\t   `module/link-response-resource`), resolved into `:resources`, and\n   369\t   the kept `:cursor` on the response stream\n   370\t   (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is appended)\n   371\t   is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its kept\n   372\t   position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's `:link-response`\n   373\t   entry retaining its `:request` beside the response side; the\n   374\t   envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand variant.\"\n   375\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   376\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\n   377\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\n   378\t        req-h (get resources (:request entry))\n   379\t        kept (:cursor entry)]\n   380\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec [(:response entry) kept] resp-h kept)]\n   381\t      (let [resp (lift-marker serve! resp-h)\n   382\t            req (lift-marker serve! req-h)]\n   383\t        (if (and resp req)\n   384\t          {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason,\n   385\t                             :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry),\n   386\t                             :yin.k/name (:name entry),\n   387\t                             :yin.k/request req,\n   388\t                             :yin.k/response resp,\n   389\t                             :yin.k/cell cid}\n   390\t                      (= :link-request reason)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
