{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '390,760p'\"","aggregated_output":"   390\t                      (= :link-request reason)\n   391\t                      (assoc :yin.k/envelope (:envelope entry))),\n   392\t           :cell? true}\n   393\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity (or req-h resp-h)))))\n   394\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))))\n   395\t\n   396\t\n   397\t(defn- lift-one\n   398\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into `{:pending data,\n   399\t   :cell? bool}` -- `:cell?` true when the variant names a cursor\n   400\t   cell, which is what puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in\n   401\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` -- or an outcome carrying\n   402\t   `:yin.k/status`: `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when a stream cannot be\n   403\t   served or a kept cursor does not survive the codec round trip;\n   404\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, naming the reason, when the entry is no\n   405\t   variant at all.\"\n   406\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   407\t  (case (:reason entry)\n   408\t    :next\n   409\t    (if (:call-id entry)\n   410\t      (lift-response-wait resources mint codec entry)\n   411\t      (lift-read resources mint codec entry))\n   412\t\n   413\t    :put\n   414\t    (if (:request-sent entry)\n   415\t      (lift-retained-request serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   416\t      (lift-write serve! resources entry))\n   417\t\n   418\t    :link-request (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   419\t\n   420\t    :link-response (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   421\t\n   422\t    :install\n   423\t    {:pending {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name (:name entry)}}\n   424\t\n   425\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable, :yin.k/reason (:reason entry)}))\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\t;; =============================================================================\n   429\t;; Lift: the frame and the single entry\n   430\t;; =============================================================================\n   431\t\n   432\t(defn lift-frame\n   433\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pending entries, lifted together:\n   434\t   `{:yin.k/pending [data ...], :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   435\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success -- the cells minted across\n   436\t   the WHOLE set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to\n   437\t   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\n   438\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` when any entry names a cell; the S7.9\n   439\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` outcome, naming the stream identity where one\n   440\t   is known, when any entry's stream cannot be served or its kept\n   441\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip; the S7.9\n   442\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcome when any entry names no variant.\n   443\t   Failure is total (S7.5.4): a refused leaf refuses the frame.\"\n   444\t  ([serve! resources entries]\n   445\t   (lift-frame serve! resources entries cursor-codec))\n   446\t  ([serve! resources entries codec]\n   447\t   (let [found (atom {:cells {}, :of {}})\n   448\t         mint (mint-cell serve! found)\n   449\t         lifted (mapv #(lift-one serve! resources mint codec %) entries)]\n   450\t     (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %) lifted)]\n   451\t       refusal\n   452\t       {:yin.k/pending (mapv :pending lifted),\n   453\t        :yin.k/cells (:cells @found),\n   454\t        :yin.k/requires (if (some :cell? lifted) requires {})}))))\n   455\t\n   456\t\n   457\t(defn lift-pending\n   458\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\n   459\t   cell table: `{:yin.k/pending data, :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   460\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success, with the same `:yin.k/\n   461\t   unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame`\n   462\t   gives. Frame assembly that shares cells across entries is\n   463\t   `lift-frame`'s.\"\n   464\t  ([serve! resources entry]\n   465\t   (lift-pending serve! resources entry cursor-codec))\n   466\t  ([serve! resources entry codec]\n   467\t   (let [r (lift-frame serve! resources [entry] codec)]\n   468\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   469\t       r\n   470\t       (assoc r :yin.k/pending (first (:yin.k/pending r)))))))\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\t;; =============================================================================\n   474\t;; Lower: back into resources and a wait-set entry\n   475\t;; =============================================================================\n   476\t\n   477\t(defn- stream-id-of\n   478\t  \"The fresh resource id the reflection of the stream `identity`\n   479\t   names stands under: derived from the identity, so two markers of\n   480\t   one stream attach once and lower shared. A receiver composing\n   481\t   these entries into a live `:resources` table re-keys them -- the\n   482\t   ids are fresh for the lowered state, the remap mechanical.\"\n   483\t  [identity]\n   484\t  (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"s-\" identity)))\n   485\t\n   486\t\n   487\t(defn- pending-markers\n   488\t  \"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\n   489\t   target of a put, the request of a retained call, the pair of a\n   490\t   link request.\"\n   491\t  [pending]\n   492\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   493\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\n   494\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)]\n   495\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   496\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   497\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   498\t    []))\n   499\t\n   500\t\n   501\t(defn- attach-all\n   502\t  \"One attach per distinct stream identity, each ok installing its\n   503\t   reflection under `stream-id-of`'s fresh resource id. The first\n   504\t   attach that does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone\n   505\t   included -- refuses the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that\n   506\t   identity.\"\n   507\t  [attach! markers]\n   508\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\n   509\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\n   510\t                      {} markers)]\n   511\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\n   512\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\n   513\t                   (let [sid (stream-id-of identity)]\n   514\t                     (-> acc\n   515\t                         (assoc-in [:streams identity] sid)\n   516\t                         (assoc-in [:resources sid] h)))\n   517\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\n   518\t               {:streams {}, :resources {}}\n   519\t               by-id)))\n   520\t\n   521\t\n   522\t(defn- cell-resources\n   523\t  \"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to: its carried\n   524\t   position, on the reflection of the stream the cell names, under the\n   525\t   cell id itself -- two references to one cell share the one entry,\n   526\t   and one ref per cell keeps its own (S7.5.3). A response-route cell\n   527\t   lowers under the engine's fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key` onto the\n   528\t   fixed `vm/call-out-stream-key` reflection instead: the restored\n   529\t   response wait reads the retried response there, so every reader of\n   530\t   the route advances the one shared entry.\"\n   531\t  [streams cells routes]\n   532\t  (into {}\n   533\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\n   534\t               (let [route? (contains? routes cid)]\n   535\t                 [(if route? vm/call-out-cursor-key cid)\n   536\t                  {:stream-id (if route?\n   537\t                                vm/call-out-stream-key\n   538\t                                (streams (cell-identity cells cid))),\n   539\t                   :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}])))\n   540\t        cells))\n   541\t\n   542\t\n   543\t(defn- route-cells\n   544\t  \"The UCF cell ids a frame's retained requests name as their\n   545\t   response route: the cells that lower under the engine's fixed\n   546\t   call-out cursor key rather than their own id, so the route's\n   547\t   readers -- the restored response wait, a co-waiting `:ffi`\n   548\t   response wait -- share the one entry (S7.5.3).\"\n   549\t  [pendings]\n   550\t  (into #{} (keep :yin.k/response-cell) pendings))\n   551\t\n   552\t\n   553\t(defn- cursor-entry-key\n   554\t  \"The resource id `cid`'s cursor entry lowers under: the cell id\n   555\t   itself, except a response-route cell -- it lowers under the\n   556\t   engine's fixed `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, the key the restored\n   557\t   response wait reads (`semantic-restore`'s own shape).\"\n   558\t  [routes cid]\n   559\t  (if (contains? routes cid) vm/call-out-cursor-key cid))\n   560\t\n   561\t\n   562\t(defn- call-pair-resources\n   563\t  \"The engine's fixed call-pair keys (`vm/call-in-stream-key`,\n   564\t   `vm/call-out-stream-key`) mapped onto the reflections a retained\n   565\t   request's retry and response use: the engine's sweep appends the\n   566\t   retained envelope at the fixed call-in key -- the reader the\n   567\t   receiver's own bridge serves -- and the restored response wait\n   568\t   reads the response at the fixed call-out key, where that bridge\n   569\t   writes it. One pair per task: every retained request of a frame\n   570\t   installs the same reflections.\"\n   571\t  [streams resources pendings cells]\n   572\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n   573\t            (if (= :ffi-request (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   574\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   575\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\n   576\t                    route-id (cell-identity cells\n   577\t                                            (:yin.k/response-cell\n   578\t                                              pending))\n   579\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\n   580\t                    route (get resources (streams route-id))]\n   581\t                (if (and req route)\n   582\t                  (assoc acc\n   583\t                         vm/call-in-stream-key req,\n   584\t                         vm/call-out-stream-key route)\n   585\t                  acc))\n   586\t              acc))\n   587\t          {}\n   588\t          pendings))\n   589\t\n   590\t\n   591\t(defn- link-pair-resources\n   592\t  \"The engine's fixed link keys (`module/link-request-resource`,\n   593\t   `module/link-response-resource`) mapped onto the reflections a\n   594\t   lowered link wait uses: the engine's sweep retries a\n   595\t   `:link-request` by appending at the fixed request key\n   596\t   (`module/append-link-request`) and polls a `:link-response` at the\n   597\t   fixed response key (`poll-link-response`), so a lowered link wait\n   598\t   parks where the engine looks. One pair per task: the identity of\n   599\t   each side rides the pending's own markers.\"\n   600\t  [streams resources pendings]\n   601\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n   602\t            (if (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n   603\t                           (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   604\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   605\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\n   606\t                    resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   607\t                                             :dao.stream/identity])\n   608\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\n   609\t                    resp (get resources (streams resp-id))]\n   610\t                (if (and req resp)\n   611\t                  (assoc acc\n   612\t                         module/link-request-resource req,\n   613\t                         module/link-response-resource resp)\n   614\t                  acc))\n   615\t              acc))\n   616\t          {}\n   617\t          pendings))\n   618\t\n   619\t\n   620\t(defn- lower-one\n   621\t  \"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\n   622\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\n   623\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\n   624\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\n   625\t   stream identity where one is known. `routes` are the frame's\n   626\t   response-route cells (`route-cells`): a wait on one reads the\n   627\t   engine's fixed call-out cursor.\"\n   628\t  [pending ctx streams cells routes]\n   629\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   630\t    :next\n   631\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   632\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   633\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   634\t                       {:reason :next,\n   635\t                        :stream-id sid,\n   636\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   637\t                                     :id (cursor-entry-key routes cid)}})}\n   638\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   639\t\n   640\t    :put\n   641\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\n   642\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   643\t      {:entry (merge ctx\n   644\t                     {:reason :put,\n   645\t                      :stream-id sid,\n   646\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\n   647\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\n   648\t\n   649\t    :ffi\n   650\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\n   651\t          cursor-id (cursor-entry-key routes cid)]\n   652\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   653\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   654\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\n   655\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   656\t                                :stream-id sid,\n   657\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   658\t                                             :id cursor-id}}\n   659\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\n   660\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\n   661\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   662\t\n   663\t    :ffi-request\n   664\t    (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   665\t                                  :dao.stream/identity])\n   666\t          route-id (cell-identity cells (:yin.k/response-cell\n   667\t                                          pending))]\n   668\t      (if (and (streams req-id) (streams route-id))\n   669\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   670\t                       {:reason :put,\n   671\t                        :request-sent true,\n   672\t                        :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   673\t                        :op (:yin.k/request-op pending),\n   674\t                        :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key,\n   675\t                        :datom (apply2/request (:yin.k/call-id pending)\n   676\t                                               (:yin.k/request-op\n   677\t                                                 pending)\n   678\t                                               (:yin.k/request-args\n   679\t                                                 pending))})}\n   680\t        (unsatisfied (if (streams req-id) route-id req-id))))\n   681\t\n   682\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   683\t    (let [reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   684\t          cid (:yin.k/cell pending)\n   685\t          sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))\n   686\t          req (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   687\t                                        :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   688\t      (if (and sid req)\n   689\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   690\t                       (cond-> {:reason reason,\n   691\t                                :link-id (:yin.k/link-id pending),\n   692\t                                :name (:yin.k/name pending),\n   693\t                                :request module/link-request-resource,\n   694\t                                :response module/link-response-resource,\n   695\t                                :cursor (:yin.k/position (get cells cid))}\n   696\t                         (= :link-request reason)\n   697\t                         (assoc :envelope (:yin.k/envelope pending))))}\n   698\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   699\t\n   700\t    :install\n   701\t    {:entry (merge ctx\n   702\t                   {:reason :install, :name (:yin.k/name pending)})}\n   703\t\n   704\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable,\n   705\t     :yin.k/reason (:yin.k/reason pending)}))\n   706\t\n   707\t\n   708\t(defn lower-frame\n   709\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pendings, lowered together:\n   710\t   `{:entries [e ...], :resources table}` -- one fresh stream entry\n   711\t   per distinct served identity and one fresh cursor entry per\n   712\t   distinct UCF cell, two waiters on one cell lowering back into one\n   713\t   shared entry and independent cells staying independent (S7.5.3) --\n   714\t   with the same `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable`\n   715\t   outcomes `lift-frame` gives. Where the engine resolves a wait at\n   716\t   one of its own fixed resource keys, the lowered reflections stand\n   717\t   under exactly those keys: a link wait's pair under\n   718\t   `module/link-request-resource` and `module/link-response-resource`,\n   719\t   a retained request's route under the engine's fixed call-pair keys\n   720\t   (`call-pair-resources`, the route cell lowering as the fixed\n   721\t   call-out cursor). `contexts`, parallel to `pendings`, is each\n   722\t   entry's register context, merged verbatim.\"\n   723\t  [attach! pendings cells contexts]\n   724\t  (let [ms (distinct (remove nil?\n   725\t                             (concat (map :yin.k/stream (vals cells))\n   726\t                                     (mapcat pending-markers pendings))))\n   727\t        a (attach-all attach! ms)]\n   728\t    (if (contains? a :yin.k/status)\n   729\t      a\n   730\t      (let [routes (route-cells pendings)\n   731\t            lowered (mapv #(lower-one %1 %2 (:streams a) cells routes)\n   732\t                          pendings contexts)]\n   733\t        (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %)\n   734\t                               lowered)]\n   735\t          refusal\n   736\t          {:entries (mapv :entry lowered),\n   737\t           :resources (merge (:resources a)\n   738\t                             (cell-resources (:streams a) cells routes)\n   739\t                             (call-pair-resources (:streams a)\n   740\t                                                  (:resources a)\n   741\t                                                  pendings cells)\n   742\t                             (link-pair-resources (:streams a)\n   743\t                                                  (:resources a)\n   744\t                                                  pendings))})))))\n   745\t\n   746\t\n   747\t(defn lower-pending\n   748\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e, :resources\n   749\t   table}` -- the wait-set entry `ctx`'s registers ride on, and the\n   750\t   fresh resource entries it polls through -- with the same\n   751\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes\n   752\t   `lower-frame` gives. Frame assembly that shares cursor entries\n   753\t   across entries is `lower-frame`'s.\"\n   754\t  [attach! pending cells ctx]\n   755\t  (let [r (lower-frame attach! [pending] cells [ctx])]\n   756\t    (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   757\t      r\n   758\t      (-> r\n   759\t          (assoc :entry (first (:entries r)))\n   760\t          (dissoc :entries)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
